<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Marj Rahit (684)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">684</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-fitna">Second Fitna</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Marj Rahit was fought in August 684 north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> between the Umayyad Marwan I, backed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-kalb">Kalb</a> tribes, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qays">Qays</a> tribes under al-Dahhak ibn Qays, who supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-allah-ibn-al-zubayr">Ibn al-Zubayr</a>. Marwan's victory secured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyads</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-fitna">Second Fitna</a> and fuelled a long feud between the Qays and Kalb tribal factions.</p></div>
